# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Branch Demo
# A short standalone scene reached via [goto] from the prologue.
# This file demonstrates how story arcs work: the prologue routes here,
# this scene plays, and then [goto] forwards the player to the epilogue.
# In a real project, this would be a chapter, a side story, or a route branch.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_branch_demo
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}

{{BG_DECL}}@label start
{{BG_START}}[show lavender right {{LAVENDER_EXPR}}]
[wait 200]

# ─── Scene ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is where your scene content goes. Right now it's a short meta-explanation,
# but in a real game this would be dialogue, narration, character staging — a full scene.

Lavender: You just arrived here via a {b}[goto]{/b} command from the prologue script.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: That command looked like this in the prologue file:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[goto {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_branch_demo:start]{/color}
narrator: The first part is the {b}@scenario ID{/b} of this file. The second part ({b}:start{/b}) is the label to jump to.

Lavender: This is a completely separate .vns file with its own @scenario declaration, its own labels, and its own content.
Lavender: The prologue doesn't know what happens inside this file — it just knows the address.

[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: Here's what makes this a {b}story arc{/b} pattern:
narrator: {b}1.{/b} The prologue presents a choice.
narrator: {b}2.{/b} The choice label contains a [goto] to this file.
narrator: {b}3.{/b} This file runs its scene from top to bottom.
narrator: {b}4.{/b} At the end, another [goto] forwards to the epilogue.
narrator: That's the chain: {color=#8888cc}prologue → branch → epilogue{/color}.

[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: You can add as many branch files as you want — one per chapter, one per route, one per side story.
Lavender: Each one is a self-contained .vns file connected by [goto] at the seams.

narrator: The next line sends you to the epilogue. Open {b}{{STORY_EPILOGUE_SCRIPT_PATH}}{/b} to see what happens there.

# ─── Forward to Epilogue ────────────────────────────────────────
# This [goto] completes the arc: prologue → this branch → epilogue.
# In a real game, you might have multiple branches that all converge on the same epilogue,
# or different epilogues for different routes.

[goto {{EPILOGUE_TARGET}}:start]
